body:
Three read-path fixes as one topic, the warm-key cut split out to #762:

1. a reader's reads are deduped once per read, under the list's generation (fixes the `seen_first` key to name the READER — two readers of one file no longer hide each other);
2. a kept verdict's reads are asked once per ATTEMPT, not once per const (`ask_kept_reads` — the read generation drives it);
3. `view_stands` is memoized per view id for the attempt (588 hits / 49 misses).

Measured (controlled stale pair, one binary/source): stale-lower delta **+58.3 s -> +7.8 s**; `view_stands` 14.3 s -> 1.0 s.

Receipts: `make cache-attacks` FAIL count 0; `avra test packages/std-avrac` 8851/8851; `fmt --check` 5 examined, 0 differing. Supersedes #751 and #755 (both stacked/fmt-red).
